---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Research and Provenance"
  description="Editorial provenance standards and publication boundaries for The Dead Air Archive."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Research</p>
      <h1>Research and Provenance</h1>
      <p>
        Public entries should identify their fictional archive status, publication history, and
        relevant content notes. Source-like language belongs to the finished work, not to private
        production material.
      </p>
      <h2>Publication Boundary</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Publish edited public-facing entries only.</li>
        <li>Do not commit raw transcripts or interview-like source material.</li>
        <li>Do not name real participants or private collaborators without explicit approval.</li>
        <li>Do not expose hidden canon, unpublished continuity, or internal research notes.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Archive Status</h2>
      <p>
        Collection entries can be marked sealed, active, fragmentary, or withheld. Withheld items
        may be referenced by public pages without exposing private notes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
